# Command aider

## What does this command do:

Aider lets you pair program with LLMs to start a new project or build on your
existing codebase.

## Installed from

Aider is the Python package `aider-chat` (PyPI). It pins `numpy==1.24.3`, which
will NOT build on Python 3.13 — install it under Python 3.12. All k-fed hosts have
`mise`, so use it to provide a 3.12 toolchain and point `pipx` at it.

For Fedora install using: mise install python@3.12 && pipx install --python "$(mise where python@3.12)/bin/python" aider-chat
For Raspberry Pi install using: mise install python@3.12 && pipx install --python "$(mise where python@3.12)/bin/python" aider-chat
For Mac install using: mise install python@3.12 && pipx install --python "$(mise where python@3.12)/bin/python" aider-chat
For Mac container (Fedora Linux, ARM/aarch64) install using: mise install python@3.12 && pipx install --python "$(mise where python@3.12)/bin/python" aider-chat

> Note: the Mac container runs Fedora Linux on ARM (aarch64), not x86_64. aider is
> a pure-Python (pipx) install, so there is no arch-specific binary to pick — the
> same command works on aarch64 and x86_64.
>
> Upgrade on any host: `pipx upgrade aider-chat`. Uninstall: `pipx uninstall aider-chat`.
> The official `aider-install` bootstrapper (`pipx run aider-install`) is an
> alternative that auto-provides its own Python 3.12 via `uv`.

## Command path

For Fedora run: ~/.local/bin/aider
For Raspberry Pi run: ~/.local/bin/aider
For Mac run: ~/.local/bin/aider
For Mac container run: ~/.local/bin/aider

